<script language="javascript" src="../../_dwr/interface/NewsvoteDWR.js"></script><script language="javascript" src="../../_dwr/engine.js"></script><script language="javascript" src="/system/resource/js/news/newscontent.js"></script><link rel="stylesheet" Content-type="text/css" href="/system/resource/style/component/news/content/format2.css"><script language="javascript" src="/system/resource/js/ajax.js"></script><form name="_newscontent_fromname">
<div class="show-news01"><h5 times new roman";" style=" font-size: 30px;color:#333333;line-height:42px;margin-bottom:10px; text-align: center">Guangzhou Institute of Technology</h5></div>
    <div id="vsb_content_2" style="margin-bottom: 40px;font-size: 18px;color: #333333;line-height:30px;text-align:justify;display: block;margin: 30px auto;max-width: 1080px; min-height:800px;"><div class="v_news_content">
<p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">Guangzhou Institute of technology is a high-level, leading, and international industry-university-research collaboration entity jointly established by Xidian University and the Guangzhou municipal government. It follows the development principles of high starting point, high standards, and high-quality operations, serving as a key initiative for Xidian University to proactively align with national strategic demands, seize opportunities in the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area, and support local economic development. The institute focuses on key areas such as integrated circuits, artificial intelligence, big data, 5G applications, the Internet of Things, and cybersecurity. The goal is to establish the Guangzhou Institute of technology as a “Star of the Bay Area”—a hub for industrial-academic collaboration and a magnet for top-tier talent in core technology fields.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">Guangzhou Institute of technology is located at 83 Zhiming Road, Guangzhou Knowledge City, Huangpu District, Guangzhou, with a total planned area of 160 acres and a construction area of approximately 300,000 square meters. It was officially put into use in 2024. The institute currently has over 200 full-time faculty members and more than 400 part-time researchers. The institute currently enrolls more than 2,000 graduate students.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">The Guangzhou Institute of technology follows the principles of “creating new spaces, implementing new ideas, and establishing new mechanisms”, bringing together resources from the government, university, enterprises, and institutions to build a high-end industrial platform based on openness, sharing, contribution, and development. It aims to leverage both Guangdong’s geographical advantages and Xidian University’s academic strengths, fostering mutual growth and synergy between the region’s innovation potential and scientific and technological expertise of Xidian.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">In terms of talent cultivation, the Guangzhou Institute of technology leverages Xidian University’s advantages and specialties in the electronic information field. It actively promotes a reform model for professional graduate education centered on improving training quality, enhancing professional competencies, strengthening practical skills, and integrating industry and education. The institute is committed to deepening the integration of industry and education, science and education, and university-local cooperation, cultivating outstanding engineering and technology talents with exceptional technological innovation capabilities and problem-solving skills. By establishing a collaborative training model involving government, industries, and universities, it aims to create a 'Bay Area Model' for the training of outstanding engineers.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">In the field of scientific research innovation and technology transfer, the Guangzhou Institute of technology adheres to the principle that national needs, social demands, and market requirements serve as both the starting point and ultimate goal. Focusing on the strategic industrial needs of Guangdong Province and Guangzhou City, the institute has established eight major research centers in semiconductors and integrated circuits, artificial intelligence, advanced manufacturing, optoelectronic information, next-generation communications, radar technology, future computing, and cybersecurity. Through organized scientific research and innovation, the institute enhances Guangzhou’s capabilities in hard technology and industrial development potential in these areas. Additionally, the Guangzhou Institute of technology has established a collaborative innovation system for technology transfer driven by enterprise demands, striving to integrate and advance the talent chain, innovation chain, industry chain, and financial chain to build the institute into a demonstration zone for technology transfer and commercialization.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">“With the tide in our favor, we set sail with full sails.” The Guangzhou Institute of technology is taking bold and innovative steps to drive industrial upgrading in the Greater Bay Area, supporting the “New Infrastructure” strategy and establishing itself as a model for industry-education integration and science-education collaboration. It aims to accelerate and enhance Xidian University’s development as a world-class institution, provide an effective example for university-local cooperation and innovation-driven education in specialized universities, and contribute to strengthening China’s scientific and technological capabilities, global competitiveness, and overall national strength in science and technology.</span></p><p style="text-align: justify; text-indent: 0em; font-size: 20px;"><span style="font-family: &quot;times new roman&quot;; font-size: 20px;">Homepage:https://gzyjy.xidian.edu.cn/</span></p>
</div></div><div id="div_vote_id"></div>
